  "titulo": "Relative clauses with the indicative or the subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "Busco al chavo que habla inglés / Busco a alguien que hable inglés.",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "In a relative clause, use the indicative when the person or thing is known or exists (el chavo que tiene ojos azules), and the subjunctive when it's unknown, hypothetical or doesn't exist (un chavo que tenga ojos azules; no hay nadie que sepa).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The mood in the **que** clause depends on whether you know the person or thing exists."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Antecedent",
            "Mood",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "known, specific, real",
              "indicative",
              "el chavo que tiene ojos azules"
            ],
            [
              "unknown, any, hypothetical",
              "subjunctive",
              "un chavo que tenga ojos azules"
            ],
            [
              "doesn't exist (nadie, nada, ningún)",
              "subjunctive",
              "no hay nadie que sepa"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Articles help: **el / la** often points to a known one; **un / una / alguien** to any one."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if you could point at them, indicative. If you're still looking, subjunctive."
        }
      ]
